दैवत्य, अस्, आ, अम् (fr. देवता), having as one's
deity, addressed to some deity, sacred to a deity;
[cf. देवत्य.]

दैवदत्त 2. दैवदत्त, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. देव-दत्त;
for 1. see under दैव, col. 2), being in the village
Deva-datta; (आस्), m. pl. the disciples of Deva-datta.

दैवराति दैवराति, इस्, m. (fr. देव-रात), a
descendant of Deva-rāta; a patronymic of Janaka;
a N. of Yājñavalkya.
